    {
      "id": "18665",
      "key": "SFCC-331",
      "summary": "Checkout – Promo Code Entry & Validation",
      "description": "As a\n Shopper, \nI want\n to enter a promotional code during checkout, \nso that\n I can apply a discount to my order before paying.\nThe promo code entry field appears in the right-hand order summary panel on the checkout page. This story covers the entry mechanism, validation feedback, confirmation messaging, applied state display (including the applied code label and Remove interaction), Apply button disable state after a successful application, and item-level discount display. Once a promo code is successfully applied, the Apply button is disabled — preventing a second code from being entered. Auto-applied discounts are handled in SFCC-38 and SFCC-42. For international (Global-e) checkouts, coupon validation occurs in SFCC before cart handoff — Global-e does not re-validate. Promotion calculations execute in the customer's selected ship-to currency.\nThis story covers the promo code entry flow and validation logic, including the input field UI, Apply/Remove interactions, error messaging, and applied state. The rendering of Was/Now pricing and item-level discount labels (e.g. \"20% off applied\") on order summary line items is not in scope here — that will be covered in the Checkout epic. The promotional banner will also be covered in the Checkout epic.\nNote: \nPromo codes are case insensitive and alphanumeric. ",
